{"text": "Home Before Dark.\n\nJonas held Paloma's shoulder and walked on one leg. They followed the old animal with the deep bell.\n\nIt was hard. The ground was wet and full of stones.\n\nPaloma gave Jonas the last piece of chocolate.\n\n\"You should eat it,\" he said.\n\n\"No. You're the one with the bad leg.\"\n\nThe old goat stopped, too. It looked back and waited for them. Then it walked on.\n\n\"I think it likes us,\" said Jonas.\n\n\"I think it wants my hat,\" said Paloma.\n\nThen the ground was different. It was flat and hard and brown.\n\n\"Jonas,\" said Paloma. \"It's the path!\"\n\nThe fog was thinner now. Paloma saw trees. Then a yellow light between the trees. Then a roof and a gate.\n\nIt was the old wooden house. Their house!\n\nThe animals went into the field behind the house, one after another. An old man stood at the gate and counted them.\n\n\"Eighteen, nineteen, twenty,\" he said. Then he looked at Paloma and Jonas. \"And two more?\"\n\nMrs Berg ran out of the house. Half the class ran behind her.\n\n\"Paloma! Jonas!\" She held them both. \"We looked for you for three hours! Are you hurt?\"\n\n\"Jonas hurt his leg,\" said Paloma. \"I'm really sorry. I left the path for a photo.\"\n\nMrs Berg looked at his leg. \"It isn't broken. You're going to be fine. But how did you find the house in this fog?\"\n\n\"We followed the goats,\" said Jonas.\n\nMrs Berg smiled for the first time. \"Of course you did. Rule four.\"\n\n\"Rule four?\" asked Paloma.\n\n\"If you are lost, listen. Follow the bells. These goats come home at six every evening. I told you this morning.\"\n\nJonas laughed. \"I heard it. Then I hurt my leg, and I forgot.\"\n\nPaloma's face went red. \"I didn't hear it. I was taking a photo of a butterfly.\"\n\nThat evening, Jonas sat by the fire. His leg was on a chair. The old man brought them hot milk. It was goat's milk, of course.\n\nPaloma looked at her photos. The white flower was beautiful, but it was not her favourite now.\n\nIn her favourite, twenty goats walked in a line through the fog. The old one was at the back. It looked straight at the camera.\n\n\"That's the best photo of the trip,\" said Jonas.\n\n\"I know,\" said Paloma. \"But next time, I'm going to listen first. Then I'm going to take the photo.\"\n\nOutside, in the dark field, a bell rang softly. Ding.", "textSha256": "744719a67657f5dfdaad76568e1c1b5cf47c871d49dff5deadd078d4581ed565", "voice_id": "EXAVITQu4vr4xnSDxMaL", "model_id": "eleven_v3", "speed": 0.95, "lang": "en", "parts": 1, "alignment": {"characters": ["H", "o", "m", "e", " ", "B", "e", "f", "o", "r", "e", " ", "D", "a", "r", "k", ".", "\n", "\n", "J", "o", "n", "a", "s", " ", "h", "e", "l", "d", " ", "P", "a", "l", "o", "m", "a", "'", "s", " ", "s", "h", "o", "u", "l", "d", "e", "r", " ", "a", "n", "d", " ", "w", "a", "l", "k", "e", "d", " ", "o", "n", " ", "o", "n", "e", " ", "l", "e", "g", ".", " ", "T", "h", "e", "y", " ", "f", "o", "l", "l", "o", "w", "e", "d", " ", "t", "h", "e", " ", "o", "l", "d", " ", "a", "n", "i", "m", "a", "l", " ", "w", "i", "t", "h", " ", "t", "h", "e", " ", "d", "e", "e", "p", " ", "b", "e", "l", "l", ".", "\n", "\n", "I", "t", " ", "w", "a", "s", " ", "h", "a", "r", "d", ".", " ", "T", "h", "e", " ", "g", "r", "o", "u", "n", "d", " ", "w", "a", "s", " ", "w", "e", "t", " ", "a", "n", "d", " ", "f", "u", "l", "l", " ", "o", "f", " ", "s", "t", "o", "n", "e", "s", ".", "\n", "\n", "P", "a", "l", "o", "m", "a", " ", "g", "a", "v", "e", " ", "J", "o", "n", "a", "s", " ", "t", "h", "e", " ", "l", "a", "s", "t", " ", "p", "i", "e", "c", "e", " ", "o", "f", " ", "c", "h", "o", "c", "o", "l", "a", "t", "e", ".", "\n", "\n", "\"", "Y", "o", "u", " ", "s", "h", "o", "u", "l", "d", " ", "e", "a", "t", " ", "i", "t", ",", "\"", " ", "h", "e", " ", "s", "a", "i", "d", ".", "\n", "\n", "\"", "N", "o", ".", " ", "Y", "o", "u", "'", "r", "e", " ", "t", "h", "e", " ", "o", "n", "e", " ", "w", "i", "t", "h", " ", "t", "h", "e", " ", "b", "a", "d", " ", "l"